    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3342"
                            type="person">Mr. Edward Morris</rs>
                        <lb/>404 A Yale Station <lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__770" type="place"
                            >New Haven</rs>, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__726" type="place"
                            >Conn.</rs></fw><dateline><date when="1946-04-17">April 17,
                        1946</date></dateline>
                    <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3342" type="person">Mr.
                        Morris</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>I have written to my friend <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2094" type="person">Dr.
                        Wolfers</rs>, Master of Pierson College, whether I could stay with him the
                    night of Wednesday <date when="1946-05-08">May 8th</date> to Thursday <date
                        when="1946-05-09">May 9th</date> and I have told him that you will get in
                    touch with him about the date of my coming to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__770"
                        type="place">New Haven</rs>. If it is <sic>allright</sic> with you that I
                    meet your group <date when="1946-05-08">Wednesday night</date> and if this fits
                        <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__2094" type="person">Dr. Wolfers</rs> with whom
                    I have to talk for quite a time also agrees with the date, we may leave it at
                    that. If you find out from him that he would prefer another day in the same week
                    it is <sic>allright</sic> with me. May I ask you to get in touch with him as
                    soon as you have received this letter and let me know the day you have decided
                    about since I have to plan an obligation in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__835"
                        type="place">New London</rs> in connection with that date.</p>
                <p>I am looking forward to seeing you again, not only in Yale but also for a more
                    important event in July in <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__769" type="place">East
                        Hampton</rs>.<!--nicht ermittelt--></p>
                <closer><salute>Cordially yours,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Prof. Paul Tillich </rs></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
